      "message": "This is incorrect. This was written under the impression that the `miter-limit` value is a limit on how far the miter can extend (the `miter-length`). However, this is not the case as `miter-limit \u003d miter-length / stroke-width`. Since this is already a ratio (and `stroke-width` is being scaled) this value should not be scaled. This resulted in https://issues.chromium.org/issues/379510433 . Part of this is the terrible documentation around the miter limit and what it does.\n\nCreated https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/946917 to fix.",
